Z||000010||Joe Torma||09-16-2001||01:29 AM||||Not that you mentioned it, but the 3400series V6 is at least 50lbs lighter than the 2.8.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/amsig.gif"> <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A>||||reg||1
Z||000011||KissMySSFiero||09-16-2001||10:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>Not that you mentioned it, but the 3400series V6 is at least 50lbs lighter than the 2.8.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>how is it lighter?  a few pounds i might see, but 50 seems high.  its the same block and heads just different bore and stoke i thought?  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000012||88formula||09-16-2001||12:24 PM||||The 3400 engine has aluminum heads, which makes it lighter.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||KissMySSFiero||09-16-2001||12:31 PM||||I didnt think you could use the alum. heads with the fiero intake?  or can you with the camero 3400?<P>88form do you have alum heads?<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000014||Joe Torma||09-16-2001||01:05 PM||||The 3400 is a FWD block.  I wouldn't use the stock Fiero intake... too restrictive.  The Aluminum GenIII heads have larger valves than all the others, fast-burn heart shaped chambers and you can pick them up with one finger.  The intake has larger ports.  I did have to engineer a few parts to put it in.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/3400.gif"> <P>Some creative scoop/vent work is necesssary on the deck lid unless you want to relocate the alternator.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joescar9.jpg"> <P>Desktop Dyno says 300hp.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Too bad I'm going to have 200lbs of stereo.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Wannabe||09-16-2001||06:12 PM||||SBC weighs approx 575 with iron heads and intake. Al heads save 80 lbs and al intake saves 25.||||reg||1
Z||000016||artherd||09-16-2001||06:19 PM||||A (dry, no fluids) Northstar weighs about 350lbs. (though a rather poor scale was used)<P>I was suprised how heavy the Getrag 5-speed is, I'd say closer to 100lbs+.<BR>(but that is just a guess from lifting one, phew. ok, I'm a wuss  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">   <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"<p>[This message has been edited by artherd (edited 09-16-2001).]||||reg||1
